makepad remote bridge: refuse browser requests and drop the wildcard CORS header (decision D10c).

The bridge (`--remote` / MAKEPAD_REMOTE) injects real input, serves screen grabs and returns every TextInput's raw
buffer. It answered every request with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` and checked nothing, so any web page open on
the machine could read /snap and fire /click on a running app. This patch:
- refuses (403) any request carrying `Origin`, `Referer` or `Sec-Fetch-*` (every browser request carries one; curl,
  urllib and the harness send none);
- refuses a `Host` that names a domain other than localhost (DNS rebinding; IP literals stay allowed for fleet boxes);
- stops sending `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.
Applied to every tree by scripts/apply-makepad-patches.sh; tests/makepad_bridge_guard.rs checks its shape.

